  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You are an engineer on the recycling robot team writing a program to train a neural network to sort recyclable items. The program holds twelve scans of training data for recyclable items, each with its weight in ounces and its transparency.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Train the network on the inputs (the scans) and the outputs (the bins).\r\n2. Predict the bin for the red can, the green bottle, and the small jar, then print each prediction beside its correct bin: Aluminum, Glass, and Glass, respectively.\r\n3. Run the program. Which predictions match the correct bins?\r\n\r\nIf you get stuck, you can ask AI Tutor for help with training the network and making a prediction.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nUse `model.fit` to train the network on a list of inputs and a list of outputs.\r\n\r\nIf `x` is one item, represented with a list of features, `model.predict([x])[0]` returns the network's prediction.\r\n",
